    {
      "id": "78037f4d-1f2f-4019-aae2-135efd1a32bd",
      "name": "Sticky - sticky-main",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1264,
        304
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": "#F3EF77",
        "width": 714,
        "height": 916,
        "content": "## **AI Email Management Agent**\n\n**Who it's for:** Anyone drowning in inbox triage who wants urgent emails flagged, replies drafted, and promotional clutter cleared automatically.\n\n**What it does:** Watches your Gmail inbox, classifies every new email by urgency, drafts a reply for anything that needs one, alerts you on Slack for the important ones, and keeps a log of everything so nothing slips through.\n\n**How it works**\n1. Gmail Trigger polls for new mail every minute\n2. Extracts sender, subject, body, and checks it hasn't been processed already\n3. Claude classifies it: Urgent, Important, Normal, or Promotional\n4. Promotional mail is labeled, archived, and logged\n5. Everything else gets an AI-drafted reply saved to Gmail Drafts\n6. Urgent/Important emails also trigger a Slack alert and an Airtable task\n7. Normal emails are logged to Sheets; every message is marked processed\n\n**How to set up**\n☐ Connect Gmail\n☐ Add an Anthropic API credential (generic header auth)\n☐ Connect Slack and set your Urgent + General channel IDs\n☐ Connect Airtable and create a Tasks table\n☐ Connect Google Sheets and create Promotional Log / Normal Log tabs\n☐ (Optional) Point the dedup-guard nodes at your own Supabase/Airtable endpoint\n\n**CUSTOMIZATION**\n- Adjust the classification categories or urgency rules\n- Change the reply-drafting tone in the AI prompt\n- Swap the Slack alert for WhatsApp/Twilio if preferred"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
